---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Add, list, remove and verify the workspace's WebAssembly plugins; scaffold and test new ones

Usage: rustman plugin [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  add     Fetch a plugin from a workspace path or an https URL, print its manifest, pin its sha256 and declare it with no grants
  list    List the workspace's plugins: version, API, grants and trust state
  remove  Remove a plugin from rustman.toml and rustman.lock
  verify  Re-hash every plugin against its pin and update rustman.lock; exits 2 on a mismatch
  api     List the plugin API versions this rustman supports
  test    Run a plugin's test cases in the sandbox, with a fake clock, randomness, environment, network and secrets; exits 1 on a failure
  new     Scaffold a plugin project for one extension point
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help

Examples:
  rustman plugin add ./plugins/hmac
  rustman plugin add https://plugins.example.com/hmac-0.2.0.wasm --name hmac
  rustman plugin list
  rustman plugin verify
  rustman plugin new my-auth --kind auth
  rustman plugin test ./my-auth
